separately. Paying an unspecified fee, making a donation, or downloading the
Software does not by itself grant commercial permission.

Commercial purposes include internal business or employer work; work for
paying clients; paid teaching or training; sale or paid distribution of the
Software or a derivative; and use in a paid conversion service, hosted service
or commercial product. This applies even when no separate conversion fee is
charged or the business has not yet made a profit. Calling a business activity
"personal use" does not make it noncommercial.

4. Rights holder and own-business exception
